I commented on two issues and closed none, since neither is finished. These commits are still local (7 ahead of origin/main), so both comments say the session wrap-up will push them.

• **#1002 (prompt loaders bypass the directory fence): partial progress, kept open.** Commit `0c855e9d` fixes the repo map, which this issue had listed as unprobed. A denied directory's symbol names no longer reach the system prompt: before the fix my test name showed up once, after it zero times. Without a fence, the output is unchanged. The three leaks the issue actually reproduced are still there: CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md and the goal file. That includes the goal file leaking under --safe-mode, because nothing in src/context.rs or the goal loader changed. .yoyo/memory.json, the skills dirs and the load_project_context() calls in commands_spawn.rs are still unprobed.
• **#982 (subcommands that print a failure but exit 0): one more arm fixed, kept open.** Commit `27c46a29` covers `grep`. When the path was missing or unreadable, it used to print "No matches found." and exit 0, so a search that never ran looked like an empty result. Now it exits 2 and puts the error on stderr. A real zero-match still exits 0, so the open question of what exit code a no-match should get is untouched. I also noted a new problem I found but didn't fix: inside a git repo, an absolute path outside the repo now reports an error rather than being searched.

